WEBVTT

1
00:49:40.834 --> 00:49:42.834
Good morning everyone.

2
00:49:44.834 --> 00:49:49.834
Since it is so pleasant, let's see if I can get it a bit more centered again.

3
00:49:49.834 --> 00:49:52.834
Yes, that works well. Thank you.

4
00:49:59.834 --> 00:50:04.834
We're going to talk about money again for a moment. Ooh, scary. Right?

5
00:50:04.834 --> 00:50:16.834
Jesus also spoke about money. Shall we read from Matthew 25, verses 14 and 15?

6
00:50:19.834 --> 00:50:31.834
This is the beginning of a parable, where Jesus uses things from daily life to explain the kingdom of God, to explain the principles of God.

7
00:50:31.834 --> 00:50:47.834
This is the beginning of such a story. It says, it is the same, says Jesus, as with a man who went abroad, apparently a very wealthy man.

8
00:50:47.834 --> 00:50:56.834
Before he went, he called his servants to him. He gave them an amount of money to do business for him.

9
00:50:56.834 --> 00:51:08.834
To one servant he gave 1200 gold coins, to another 500 gold coins, to a third 250 gold coins.

10
00:51:08.834 --> 00:51:18.834
He gave each the amount of money he knew that servant could handle well. Then he went on his journey.

11
00:51:19.834 --> 00:51:37.834
A few managers are appointed to advance the business while the owner departs abroad, and it says that he eventually returned after a long time.

12
00:51:38.834 --> 00:51:47.834
This is about a lot of money. A lot. Not just a little.

13
00:51:47.834 --> 00:51:58.834
That shows an enormous trust. But with great trust also comes serious responsibility.

14
00:51:59.834 --> 00:52:12.834
It works the same way when you're at work. If you receive great trust for important matters, important decisions, or perhaps very expensive machines.

15
00:52:15.834 --> 00:52:25.834
I once worked with a device. You held it in your hands and it cost 100,000 euros. You shouldn't stumble at such a moment. It's not wise.

16
00:52:26.834 --> 00:52:32.834
Great trust and great responsibility.

17
00:52:33.834 --> 00:52:40.834
In our older translation, this is called the parable of the talents.

18
00:52:41.834 --> 00:52:48.834
At that moment, the explanation almost automatically goes to the talents you have.

19
00:52:48.834 --> 00:52:57.834
Of course, that is also true. We have received all sorts of things. In talents, in time, in opportunities. But also in money.

20
00:52:57.834 --> 00:52:59.834
And here it simply states money.

21
00:53:00.834 --> 00:53:10.834
And God says, He gives everyone what is fitting, of which He knows that you can handle it.

22
00:53:12.834 --> 00:53:17.834
And then the task is to handle it well.

23
00:53:17.834 --> 00:53:23.834
They do not need to be afraid that we are burdened with an impossible load. Not at all.

24
00:53:24.834 --> 00:53:31.834
For God gives so much, of which He knows that you can handle it well.

25
00:53:32.834 --> 00:53:39.834
Isn't that beautiful? Isn't that reassuring? But He also gives a lot.

26
00:53:39.834 --> 00:53:42.834
For He trusts us as well.

27
00:53:43.834 --> 00:53:46.834
And you know, it is not about how much you have.

28
00:53:46.834 --> 00:53:52.834
For the servants who acted well at the end of the story.

29
00:53:53.834 --> 00:53:56.834
One has earned a lot, the other has earned even more.

30
00:53:56.834 --> 00:53:59.834
Both receive the same reward.

31
00:54:00.834 --> 00:54:07.834
A beautiful, good, eternal life with Christ. The same reward.

32
00:54:08.834 --> 00:54:15.834
Shall we then, and that is the challenge for today, handle responsibly and well.

33
00:54:15.834 --> 00:54:18.834
With what has been made available to us.

34
00:54:19.834 --> 00:54:22.834
For everything has been made available by God.

35
00:54:23.834 --> 00:54:25.834
For we live for Him.

36
00:54:26.834 --> 00:54:30.834
You have the opportunity to contribute to the collections when there are guests.

37
00:54:31.834 --> 00:54:33.834
We generally do that with a QR code.

38
00:54:34.834 --> 00:54:38.834
Through our Open Church app. Own app Open Church.

39
00:54:39.834 --> 00:54:42.834
Or simply via a bank transfer.

40
00:54:42.834 --> 00:54:45.834
But guests, you may also feel like a guest.

41
00:54:46.834 --> 00:54:52.834
Those who are at home here, we expect them to contribute to the functioning of the church.

42
00:54:53.834 --> 00:54:54.834
Thank you very much.

43
00:55:12.834 --> 00:55:14.834
The microphone is quite handy.

44
00:55:18.834 --> 00:55:25.834
Through Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, God established the people of Israel.

45
00:55:26.834 --> 00:55:31.834
He intended to set apart a people in the world.

46
00:55:31.834 --> 00:55:38.834
To show that when a people lives in their own way, how it can go with a people.

47
00:55:39.834 --> 00:55:41.834
He intended to showcase them.

48
00:55:42.834 --> 00:55:44.834
But it turned out a bit differently.

49
00:55:45.834 --> 00:55:49.834
This year we have read a lot together in Chronicles.

50
00:55:50.834 --> 00:55:53.834
And you see how the people of Israel bounce in all directions.

51
00:55:54.834 --> 00:55:57.834
Every now and then there was a good king, not many.

52
00:55:58.834 --> 00:56:00.834
And then he led the people towards God.

53
00:56:01.834 --> 00:56:03.834
And then it went well with the people.

54
00:56:04.834 --> 00:56:05.834
Because they sought God.

55
00:56:06.834 --> 00:56:08.834
But most kings made a mess of it.

56
00:56:09.834 --> 00:56:10.834
They started to throw off praying.

57
00:56:10.834 --> 00:56:11.834
The people joined in.

58
00:56:12.834 --> 00:56:13.834
It became a mess.

59
00:56:14.834 --> 00:56:15.834
And it really became a mess.

60
00:56:16.834 --> 00:56:19.834
The people of Israel are oppressed by Egypt.

61
00:56:20.834 --> 00:56:21.834
Through Babylon.

62
00:56:22.834 --> 00:56:23.834
Through Assyria.

63
00:56:24.834 --> 00:56:25.834
Through Persia.

64
00:56:26.834 --> 00:56:29.834
Later also through the Greeks and the Romans and the Germans.

65
00:56:32.834 --> 00:56:33.834
Why?

66
00:56:34.834 --> 00:56:35.834
There was a king.

67
00:56:36.834 --> 00:56:38.834
We have talked a lot about this this year.

68
00:56:39.834 --> 00:56:40.834
His name was David.

69
00:56:41.834 --> 00:56:43.834
And under him, things went in the right direction.

70
00:56:44.834 --> 00:56:45.834
For he loved God.

71
00:56:46.834 --> 00:56:47.834
He sought God.

72
00:56:48.834 --> 00:56:49.834
And he cast away.

73
00:56:50.834 --> 00:56:52.834
And he led the people back to God.

74
00:56:53.834 --> 00:56:54.834
And he confronted the enemies.

75
00:56:55.834 --> 00:56:57.834
And there was peace in the land.

76
00:56:58.834 --> 00:57:01.834
And finally, what the people had envisioned.

77
00:57:02.834 --> 00:57:03.834
Was happening.

78
00:57:04.834 --> 00:57:08.834
And under his son Solomon, there came a beautiful time of peace and abundance.

79
00:57:09.834 --> 00:57:10.834
As God intended it.

80
00:57:11.834 --> 00:57:14.834
But soon after Solomon, things went wrong again.

81
00:57:15.834 --> 00:57:17.834
Time and again, Israel came out of misery.

82
00:57:18.834 --> 00:57:21.834
But Israel also knew that there was a promise.

83
00:57:22.834 --> 00:57:24.834
Of a king who would come after David.

84
00:57:25.834 --> 00:57:26.834
The Messiah.

85
00:57:26.834 --> 00:57:29.834
They knew of a descendant of David.

86
00:57:30.834 --> 00:57:31.834
Is going to come.

87
00:57:32.834 --> 00:57:33.834
He is our Redeemer.

88
00:57:34.834 --> 00:57:35.834
He is our Messiah.

89
00:57:36.834 --> 00:57:37.834
And when he comes.

90
00:57:38.834 --> 00:57:39.834
Then everything will be alright.

91
00:57:40.834 --> 00:57:43.834
Then we as a people will know peace.

92
00:57:48.834 --> 00:57:49.834
Centuries pass.

93
00:57:50.834 --> 00:57:54.834
In the meantime, there is again a people that overflows Israel.

94
00:57:54.834 --> 00:57:56.834
The Romans have occupied the land.

95
00:57:57.834 --> 00:58:01.834
And they are under the control and pressure of the Romans.

96
00:58:02.834 --> 00:58:03.834
And then Jesus comes.

97
00:58:05.834 --> 00:58:11.834
And Jesus tells very different things than what the people had ever heard.

98
00:58:12.834 --> 00:58:15.834
Very special things that made them think deeply.

99
00:58:16.834 --> 00:58:18.834
Very different from what they heard in the synagogue.

100
00:58:19.834 --> 00:58:20.834
And Jesus performed miracles.

101
00:58:20.834 --> 00:58:22.834
Could this be the Messiah?

102
00:58:23.834 --> 00:58:25.834
Could this be our Redeemer?

103
00:58:26.834 --> 00:58:28.834
Has the Messiah finally come?

104
00:58:29.834 --> 00:58:35.834
And then comes a day when Jesus rides into Jerusalem on a donkey.

105
00:58:37.834 --> 00:58:41.834
And the people break off palm branches from the trees.

106
00:58:42.834 --> 00:58:44.834
They throw them on the street as a tribute.

107
00:58:45.834 --> 00:58:46.834
What they always did for kings.

108
00:58:46.834 --> 00:58:48.834
When they returned from battle.

109
00:58:49.834 --> 00:58:51.834
They throw their cloaks on the road.

110
00:58:52.834 --> 00:58:54.834
And they shout, Hosanna, save us.

111
00:58:55.834 --> 00:58:56.834
Hosanna, save us.

112
00:58:58.834 --> 00:59:01.834
Okay, it's a bit strange that he rides on a donkey.

113
00:59:02.834 --> 00:59:05.834
But well, could this really be the Messiah?

114
00:59:06.834 --> 00:59:08.834
Is he finally coming to set us free?

115
00:59:09.834 --> 00:59:12.834
But then a few days later he is arrested.

116
00:59:12.834 --> 00:59:18.834
He is... gets whipped until his body is completely open.

117
00:59:19.834 --> 00:59:21.834
He is laughed at, spat upon.

118
00:59:22.834 --> 00:59:23.834
Mocked.

119
00:59:25.834 --> 00:59:27.834
And he does not open his mouth.

120
00:59:29.834 --> 00:59:30.834
And then...

121
00:59:32.834 --> 00:59:34.834
they nail him to a cross.

122
00:59:35.834 --> 00:59:36.834
And he dies.

123
00:59:37.834 --> 00:59:40.834
What a bitter disappointment.

124
00:59:41.834 --> 00:59:43.834
They had hoped so much that this was the Messiah.

125
00:59:44.834 --> 00:59:47.834
They had hoped so much that now finally the moment would come...

126
00:59:48.834 --> 00:59:51.834
that God would establish his kingdom of peace in Israel.

127
00:59:52.834 --> 00:59:54.834
But no, he dies on a cross.

128
00:59:55.834 --> 00:59:59.834
And even stronger, they are so disappointed that Jesus...

129
00:59:59.834 --> 01:00:01.834
that he stands there before Pilate.

130
01:00:02.834 --> 01:00:05.834
That they think, no, this is not the Messiah.

131
01:00:06.834 --> 01:00:08.834
Imposter. He had such beautiful words.

132
01:00:09.834 --> 01:00:11.834
Get rid of him! Crucify him!

133
01:00:12.834 --> 01:00:15.834
The same people who shouted Hosanna a few days ago.

134
01:00:16.834 --> 01:00:18.834
And threw their cloaks on the street.

135
01:00:21.834 --> 01:00:22.834
And then...

136
01:00:22.834 --> 01:00:24.834
you could say, foolish Israelites.

137
01:00:26.834 --> 01:00:28.834
He didn't realize what was going on here.

138
01:00:29.834 --> 01:00:31.834
But let's take an honest look at ourselves.

139
01:00:32.834 --> 01:00:33.834
How do we look at Jesus?

140
01:00:35.834 --> 01:00:37.834
They had, the people of Israel had their hope...

141
01:00:38.834 --> 01:00:42.834
to the Messiah who would come to solve their problems.

142
01:00:43.834 --> 01:00:45.834
And they had a lot of hope in Jesus.

143
01:00:46.834 --> 01:00:48.834
And they had a lot of hope in Jesus.

144
01:00:48.834 --> 01:00:52.834
And they had a lot of hope in the Messiah who would come to solve their problems.

145
01:00:53.834 --> 01:00:55.834
But do we not often look at Jesus in the same way?

146
01:00:56.834 --> 01:00:59.834
Hosanna, save me Jesus, help me Jesus.

147
01:01:00.834 --> 01:01:01.834
Solve my problems.

148
01:01:02.834 --> 01:01:04.834
Heal me. Hosanna, save me Jesus.

149
01:01:06.834 --> 01:01:08.834
Solve my financial problems.

150
01:01:10.834 --> 01:01:12.834
Make my wife do what I want.

151
01:01:19.834 --> 01:01:21.834
Why are You doing nothing, God?

152
01:01:22.834 --> 01:01:24.834
Where are You? Why must I wait so long?

153
01:01:25.834 --> 01:01:27.834
Why do You not answer my prayers?

154
01:01:28.834 --> 01:01:32.834
It is a bit of the same Hosanna attitude that the people of Israel had.

155
01:01:33.834 --> 01:01:35.834
Focus on, save me, help me.

156
01:01:36.834 --> 01:01:38.834
What is going on here?

157
01:01:39.834 --> 01:01:41.834
Why is this happening like this?

158
01:01:42.834 --> 01:01:43.834
Let's take a look...

159
01:01:44.834 --> 01:01:45.834
No.

160
01:01:46.834 --> 01:01:47.834
Why...

161
01:01:48.834 --> 01:01:50.834
What is the perspective here?

162
01:01:51.834 --> 01:01:53.834
Why are we actually here on earth?

163
01:01:54.834 --> 01:01:56.834
Why did God create us?

164
01:02:02.834 --> 01:02:05.834
Why did He choose the people of Israel?

165
01:02:06.834 --> 01:02:08.834
What is His plan then if...

166
01:02:08.834 --> 01:02:11.834
...things turned out so differently than what the people thought it would?

167
01:02:12.834 --> 01:02:13.834
Where is God's heart?

168
01:02:14.834 --> 01:02:16.834
Let's read in Hosea 2.

169
01:02:17.834 --> 01:02:18.834
Verse 15.

170
01:02:23.834 --> 01:02:24.834
What did I say?

171
01:02:26.834 --> 01:02:27.834
Yes.

172
01:02:28.834 --> 01:02:29.834
Breakthrough about Hosea.

173
01:02:29.834 --> 01:02:30.834
What am I saying?

174
01:02:32.834 --> 01:02:33.834
Yes.

175
01:02:33.834 --> 01:02:35.834
Breakthrough about Hosea.

176
01:02:59.834 --> 01:03:03.834
To make my bride anew by showing you that I am faithful.

177
01:03:03.834 --> 01:03:05.834
You will truly come to know me.

178
01:03:05.834 --> 01:03:10.834
This was prophesied by Hosea centuries before Jesus came.

179
01:03:12.834 --> 01:03:14.834
And then we go to Revelation.

180
01:03:14.834 --> 01:03:18.834
For John saw where it all is going to lead.

181
01:03:18.834 --> 01:03:21.834
In Revelation 21 it says.

182
01:03:21.834 --> 01:03:24.834
And I saw a new heaven and a new earth.

183
01:03:24.834 --> 01:03:28.834
For the first heaven and the first earth had passed away.

184
01:03:28.834 --> 01:03:30.834
And the sea was no more.

185
01:03:30.834 --> 01:03:37.834
And I, John, saw the holy city, the new Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God.

186
01:03:37.834 --> 01:03:42.834
It looked like a bride adorned for her husband.

187
01:03:42.834 --> 01:03:45.834
From heaven I heard a loud voice saying.

188
01:03:45.834 --> 01:03:50.834
This is the place where God will dwell with mankind.

189
01:03:50.834 --> 01:03:52.834
They will be His people.

190
01:03:52.834 --> 01:03:54.834
God Himself will be with them.

191
01:03:54.834 --> 01:03:56.834
He will be their God.

192
01:03:56.834 --> 01:03:59.834
He will wipe every tear from their eyes.

193
01:03:59.834 --> 01:04:01.834
And death will be no more.

194
01:04:01.834 --> 01:04:05.834
Neither shall there be mourning, nor crying, nor pain anymore.

195
01:04:05.834 --> 01:04:08.834
For the former things have passed away.

196
01:04:08.834 --> 01:04:10.834
And he who sat on the throne said.

197
01:04:10.834 --> 01:04:12.834
Behold, I make all things new.

198
01:04:12.834 --> 01:04:15.834
Write this down, for these words are trustworthy and true.

199
01:04:15.834 --> 01:04:17.834
I will do what I have promised.

200
01:04:17.834 --> 01:04:19.834


201
01:04:21.834 --> 01:04:25.834
Here God speaks about His bride.

202
01:04:25.834 --> 01:04:28.834
That is her final destination.

203
01:04:28.834 --> 01:04:33.834
That we, as His bride, will marry Him.

204
01:04:35.834 --> 01:04:38.834
The bride is the congregation.

205
01:04:38.834 --> 01:04:42.834
There are many synonyms for the congregation.

206
01:04:42.834 --> 01:04:46.834
The bride, the house of God, the family of God.

207
01:04:46.834 --> 01:04:49.834
The body of Christ.

208
01:04:49.834 --> 01:04:52.834
The people of Israel, the new Jerusalem.

209
01:04:52.834 --> 01:04:54.834
Is actually all the same.

210
01:04:54.834 --> 01:05:02.834
That is us together as followers, as beloved of Jesus.

211
01:05:02.834 --> 01:05:05.834
All people on earth are destined.

212
01:05:05.834 --> 01:05:11.834
And you too, chosen by God, conceived by God, created by God.

213
01:05:11.834 --> 01:05:13.834
To be His bride.

214
01:05:16.834 --> 01:05:18.834
He wants to marry you.

215
01:05:18.834 --> 01:05:23.834
He wants to marry us together, as His bride.

216
01:05:23.834 --> 01:05:29.834
He does not just want us to be His children, to be His friends.

217
01:05:29.834 --> 01:05:33.834
But He wants us to be His bride, to be His wife.

218
01:05:33.834 --> 01:05:35.834
And this is the final destination.

219
01:05:35.834 --> 01:05:38.834
This is what we were made for.

220
01:05:38.834 --> 01:05:41.834
This is what we are now going through in an earthly adventure.

221
01:05:41.834 --> 01:05:45.834
On the way to Jesus.

222
01:05:45.834 --> 01:05:49.834
When he returns, to be held back by him.

223
01:05:49.834 --> 01:05:51.834
As his bride.

224
01:05:51.834 --> 01:05:55.834
And then we will have the wedding feast.

225
01:05:55.834 --> 01:05:57.834
And then he will marry us.

226
01:05:57.834 --> 01:06:04.834
And then we will be so united with him, intertwined, entangled.

227
01:06:04.834 --> 01:06:08.834
That we will be intimately with him forever.

228
01:06:10.834 --> 01:06:12.834
And this is God's perspective.

229
01:06:12.834 --> 01:06:15.834
This is what God has in mind.

230
01:06:15.834 --> 01:06:18.834
This is why God does things.

231
01:06:21.834 --> 01:06:26.834
Does that mean that God is not interested in our problems?

232
01:06:26.834 --> 01:06:28.834
In how things are going here on earth?

233
01:06:28.834 --> 01:06:29.834
Of course he is.

234
01:06:29.834 --> 01:06:32.834
He made you. He wants the very best for you.

235
01:06:32.834 --> 01:06:36.834
Only his perspective is different from our perspective.

236
01:06:36.834 --> 01:06:40.834
We can be very caught up in our problems, our things.

237
01:06:40.834 --> 01:06:42.834
How we are doing here on earth.

238
01:06:42.834 --> 01:06:48.834
But God is very much concerned whether we are on our way to be his bride.

239
01:06:48.834 --> 01:06:51.834
Whether we are on our way to marry him.

240
01:06:51.834 --> 01:06:54.834
Whether we are on our way to be with him forever.

241
01:06:54.834 --> 01:06:57.834
God is very focused on that.

242
01:07:00.834 --> 01:07:07.834
And that is a very different perspective than when we are caught up in our narrow thinking and seeing

243
01:07:07.834 --> 01:07:10.834
dealing with our earthly problems.

244
01:07:10.834 --> 01:07:16.834
We need to make a shift from our earthly vision to the heavenly vision.

245
01:07:16.834 --> 01:07:19.834
Towards God's plan. Towards what we are searching for.

246
01:07:19.834 --> 01:07:21.834
And that is not so simple.

247
01:07:21.834 --> 01:07:24.834
The disciples struggle with that too.

248
01:07:24.834 --> 01:07:27.834
We will read about this in Acts 1 verse 6.

249
01:07:27.834 --> 01:07:29.834
This is really amazing.

250
01:07:29.834 --> 01:07:32.834
Jesus had died on a cross.

251
01:07:32.834 --> 01:07:34.834
He had risen from the dead.

252
01:07:34.834 --> 01:07:37.834
He came back to his disciples.

253
01:07:37.834 --> 01:07:39.834
With his glorified body.

254
01:07:39.834 --> 01:07:42.834
And he begins to explain how it will go on now.

255
01:07:42.834 --> 01:07:45.834
And then he says, I must go away now.

256
01:07:45.834 --> 01:07:47.834
And they do not want that.

257
01:07:47.834 --> 01:07:49.834
Jesus is always with us.

258
01:07:49.834 --> 01:07:51.834
No, says Jesus, there is something better.

259
01:07:51.834 --> 01:07:53.834
The Holy Spirit is going to come.

260
01:07:53.834 --> 01:07:55.834
I am going away.

261
01:07:55.834 --> 01:07:57.834
And the Holy Spirit is going to come.

262
01:07:57.834 --> 01:07:59.834
He just said that.

263
01:07:59.834 --> 01:08:01.834
Do you know what their answer is?

264
01:08:01.834 --> 01:08:03.834
This.

265
01:08:03.834 --> 01:08:06.834
The people who were with him asked him.

266
01:08:06.834 --> 01:08:11.834
Lord, are you now going to ensure that Israel becomes its own kingdom again?

267
01:08:11.834 --> 01:08:14.834
Then you have the Hosanna again.

268
01:08:14.834 --> 01:08:18.834
Okay, Jesus is the Messiah. He has risen from the dead.

269
01:08:18.834 --> 01:08:22.834
But are the Romans finally going to be kicked out now?

270
01:08:22.834 --> 01:08:25.834
And are we finally going to start our kingdom of peace now?

271
01:08:25.834 --> 01:08:29.834
So they haven't grasped it at all.

272
01:08:29.834 --> 01:08:31.834
And it's not that simple either.

273
01:08:31.834 --> 01:08:34.834
It's a lifelong journey that we must take.

274
01:08:34.834 --> 01:08:36.834
After our repentance.

275
01:08:36.834 --> 01:08:38.834
Together with Jesus on the way to him.

276
01:08:38.834 --> 01:08:41.834
We need to learn to make that shift.

277
01:08:41.834 --> 01:08:43.834
From earthly thinking to heavenly thinking.

278
01:08:47.834 --> 01:08:50.834
The apostles had a nice word for that.

279
01:08:50.834 --> 01:08:52.834
That focus.

280
01:08:52.834 --> 01:08:54.834
And that is Maranatha.

281
01:08:54.834 --> 01:08:57.834
We sometimes sing that. Maranatha, come Lord Jesus.

282
01:08:57.834 --> 01:09:01.834
Maranatha means, come Lord Jesus.

283
01:09:01.834 --> 01:09:04.834
You wouldn't say it.

284
01:09:04.834 --> 01:09:07.834
But that is what it literally means.

285
01:09:07.834 --> 01:09:10.834
So Hosanna means, help me, save me.

286
01:09:10.834 --> 01:09:14.834
And Maranatha means, come Jesus.

287
01:09:14.834 --> 01:09:18.834
And the title of my sermon is From Hosanna to Maranatha.

288
01:09:18.834 --> 01:09:24.834
Making the shift from, God, we need you.

289
01:09:24.834 --> 01:09:27.834
Solve our problems, to God.

290
01:09:27.834 --> 01:09:30.834
We are ready to live for you as our bride.

291
01:09:30.834 --> 01:09:33.834
We want to prepare for your return.

292
01:09:33.834 --> 01:09:38.834
We want to prepare as your fiancée for the great feast.

293
01:09:38.834 --> 01:09:40.834
How?

294
01:09:40.834 --> 01:09:46.834
We will read that in Ephesians 5, verse 25.

295
01:09:46.834 --> 01:09:50.834
Tim will be covering Ephesians in the coming time.

296
01:09:50.834 --> 01:09:53.834
So he will also be beautifully addressed again.

297
01:09:53.834 --> 01:09:59.834
Husbands, love your wives in the same way that Christ loves his congregation.

298
01:10:04.834 --> 01:10:07.834
He sacrificed himself for the congregation.

299
01:10:07.834 --> 01:10:09.834
He died on a cross.

300
01:10:09.834 --> 01:10:12.834
For you, for the congregation, for his bride.

301
01:10:12.834 --> 01:10:17.834
He has cleansed the congregation by bathing her in the Word.

302
01:10:17.834 --> 01:10:20.834
Be engaged with the Bible.

303
01:10:20.834 --> 01:10:23.834
Thus the congregation could become His possession.

304
01:10:23.834 --> 01:10:27.834
And now the congregation can become His possession.

305
01:10:28.834 --> 01:10:32.834
Thus the congregation could become His possession.

306
01:10:32.834 --> 01:10:38.834
And now the congregation can stand before Him without a single spot or wrinkle, radiant.

307
01:10:38.834 --> 01:10:41.834
Thus the congregation is completely pure.

308
01:10:41.834 --> 01:10:46.834
It is written in the books that the man and his wife are one together.

309
01:10:46.834 --> 01:10:52.834
Therefore a man shall leave his father and mother and hold fast to his wife and be faithful to her.

310
01:10:52.834 --> 01:10:56.834
From that moment they are one whole.

311
01:10:56.834 --> 01:10:59.834
That has a hidden meaning.

312
01:10:59.834 --> 01:11:05.834
I tell you that this is about the unity of Christ and His congregation.

313
01:11:05.834 --> 01:11:11.834
That hidden meaning is truly a mystery.

314
01:11:11.834 --> 01:11:16.834
It is something that the world does not understand and is under full attack.

315
01:11:16.834 --> 01:11:21.834
But marriage is not just something that people have invented.

316
01:11:21.834 --> 01:11:25.834
Or something that has worked well in history.

317
01:11:25.834 --> 01:11:34.834
No, marriage was created by God as a picture of Him with His congregation.

318
01:11:34.834 --> 01:11:37.834
That He is going to marry us.

319
01:11:37.834 --> 01:11:43.834
We have read, Hosea already says, God wants to be our man, our husband.

320
01:11:43.834 --> 01:11:45.834
God wants to marry us.

321
01:11:45.834 --> 01:11:48.834
So God is the man, we as a congregation are the woman.

322
01:11:48.834 --> 01:11:51.834
And together we will be one forever.

323
01:11:51.834 --> 01:11:56.834
That is also what you do in marriage as man and woman.

324
01:11:56.834 --> 01:11:58.834
That you go together.

325
01:11:58.834 --> 01:12:02.834
Do you find it strange that God says no one should separate that?

326
01:12:02.834 --> 01:12:07.834
Do you find it strange that marriage is so under attack in this world?

327
01:12:07.834 --> 01:12:10.834
That more and more young people decide not to get married?

328
01:12:10.834 --> 01:12:15.834
That more and more people just get divorced when it’s no longer fun or becomes difficult?

329
01:12:15.834 --> 01:12:18.834
Marriage is between man and woman.

330
01:12:18.834 --> 01:12:22.834
Do you find it strange that there is so much contention about being man and woman?

331
01:12:22.834 --> 01:12:27.834
About how you live together or in what form?

332
01:12:27.834 --> 01:12:30.834
So all of this, not just something.

333
01:12:30.834 --> 01:12:36.834
That is an attack on God's image of where we are all heading together.

334
01:12:36.834 --> 01:12:41.834
And sex is something very beautiful and something very intimate.

335
01:12:41.834 --> 01:12:44.834
Did God not create it just like that?

336
01:12:44.834 --> 01:12:52.834
It has a purpose that shows how wonderful the intimacy with God will be later.

337
01:12:52.834 --> 01:12:58.834
Sex is a picture of how intimate we will be with Him later.

338
01:12:58.834 --> 01:13:02.834
But it must be within marriage in God's way.

339
01:13:02.834 --> 01:13:07.834
Not from lust, not from self-interest or your own pleasures.

340
01:13:07.834 --> 01:13:11.834
But from love and intimacy cherishing each other.

341
01:13:11.834 --> 01:13:13.834
Then sex is so beautiful.

342
01:13:13.834 --> 01:13:18.834
And that is why sex is also so enormously under attack.

343
01:13:18.834 --> 01:13:20.834
And that is why porn is so terrible.

344
01:13:20.834 --> 01:13:25.834
For it is a violation of God's image of intimacy.

345
01:13:25.834 --> 01:13:27.834
That of what we will have with Him.

346
01:13:32.834 --> 01:13:37.834
So we have read that Jesus died on a cross.

347
01:13:37.834 --> 01:13:39.834
That was first necessary.

348
01:13:39.834 --> 01:13:42.834
Because without His, we can never ever marry Him.

349
01:13:42.834 --> 01:13:51.834
God will not marry a limp, weak, dirty, adulterous, whatever little woman.

350
01:13:51.834 --> 01:13:54.834
He will marry a perfect bride.

351
01:13:54.834 --> 01:13:56.834
Without spot or wrinkle.

352
01:13:56.834 --> 01:13:57.834
Without sin.

353
01:13:57.834 --> 01:13:59.834
Isn't that logical?

354
01:13:59.834 --> 01:14:02.834
He is God. He is completely perfect and holy.

355
01:14:02.834 --> 01:14:08.834
He is worth nothing less than the most perfect bride you can imagine.

356
01:14:08.834 --> 01:14:10.834
And that is what we must strive for.

357
01:14:10.834 --> 01:14:13.834
And that is God's perspective.

358
01:14:13.834 --> 01:14:16.834
For that, He had to die on a cross first.

359
01:14:16.834 --> 01:14:27.834
For that, we must go through our earthly period, our whole life long, to be prepared as His fiancée for the great wedding feast.

360
01:14:27.834 --> 01:14:31.834
That is why things go as they do.

361
01:14:31.834 --> 01:14:37.834
Therefore, it seems as if God is doing nothing, while He is doing everything.

362
01:14:37.834 --> 01:14:41.834
Because something very different is happening.

363
01:14:44.834 --> 01:14:46.834
We need to be cleansed.

364
01:14:46.834 --> 01:14:48.834
That is the period we are in now.

365
01:14:48.834 --> 01:14:50.834
We need to be perfect.

366
01:14:50.834 --> 01:14:52.834
Without spot or wrinkle.

367
01:14:52.834 --> 01:14:54.834
And that doesn't happen just like that.

368
01:14:54.834 --> 01:14:57.834
We cannot just flip a switch for that.

369
01:14:57.834 --> 01:14:59.834
God cannot just flip a switch for that either.

370
01:14:59.834 --> 01:15:01.834
A lot has to happen for that.

371
01:15:01.834 --> 01:15:04.834
We need our whole lives for that.

372
01:15:05.834 --> 01:15:13.834
So God is allowing things to happen in our lives, however you want to put it.

373
01:15:13.834 --> 01:15:15.834
That are not always very pleasant.

374
01:15:15.834 --> 01:15:17.834
But they do have a purpose.

375
01:15:17.834 --> 01:15:21.834
Are there any fans of the Tour de France here?

376
01:15:21.834 --> 01:15:25.834
No one? Then I am the only one.

377
01:15:25.834 --> 01:15:27.834
I am special.

378
01:15:28.834 --> 01:15:37.834
You have seen that when cyclists crash, quite a lot happens.

379
01:15:37.834 --> 01:15:41.834
That their arm is completely laid open like this.

380
01:15:41.834 --> 01:15:43.834
A gigantic abrasion.

381
01:15:43.834 --> 01:15:49.834
Do you know what happens in the evening after the finish when they have arrived?

382
01:15:49.834 --> 01:15:53.834
Then the caretaker comes with a nail brush.

383
01:15:54.834 --> 01:15:59.834
And he goes over that abrasion, just like that.

384
01:15:59.834 --> 01:16:03.834
Because, super important, all dirt must come out.

385
01:16:03.834 --> 01:16:11.834
If dirt doesn't come out, it will get infected and then it's the end of the story for that runner's performance.

386
01:16:11.834 --> 01:16:19.834
So then it goes with force and clumsiness, and that does a gigantic hurt, over that abrasion until all the dirt is out.

387
01:16:19.834 --> 01:16:21.834
And then ointment over it, and so on.

388
01:16:21.834 --> 01:16:23.834
And that's not fun.

389
01:16:23.834 --> 01:16:29.834
Then you can tell that caretaker, no, we won't do it like that next time.

390
01:16:29.834 --> 01:16:31.834
But it has to be done.

391
01:16:31.834 --> 01:16:37.834
And so there can also be things in our lives that may not be so pleasant, but are necessary.

392
01:16:37.834 --> 01:16:39.834
Otherwise, we won't make it.

393
01:16:39.834 --> 01:16:45.834
Think of pruning.

394
01:16:46.834 --> 01:16:56.834
Fruit trees need to be pruned, because when they are pruned, they bear better, larger, and more fruit afterwards.

395
01:16:56.834 --> 01:17:00.834
The Bible also speaks about this, that we need to be pruned.

396
01:17:00.834 --> 01:17:02.834
That's not fun, but it's necessary.

397
01:17:02.834 --> 01:17:08.834
It is part of preparing for His return, for becoming perfect as His bride.

398
01:17:08.834 --> 01:17:10.834
Or they purify gold.

399
01:17:10.834 --> 01:17:14.834
When they have found gold, there is all kinds of dirt and junk in it.

400
01:17:14.834 --> 01:17:18.834
And then they throw it in a pan and heat it up to a glowing temperature.

401
01:17:18.834 --> 01:17:23.834
And then the dirt rises to the surface on that gold and they can scrape it off.

402
01:17:23.834 --> 01:17:24.834
Then you get pure gold.

403
01:17:24.834 --> 01:17:26.834
The Bible also speaks about that.

404
01:17:26.834 --> 01:17:29.834
It's not fun when you are stirred up like that.

405
01:17:29.834 --> 01:17:34.834
But it is necessary, because that dirt has to come out, because you need to be perfect for Jesus.

406
01:17:35.834 --> 01:17:43.834
Even people who do fitness know that you have to endure pain to get better muscles, to become stronger.

407
01:17:43.834 --> 01:17:47.834
So it doesn't just happen by itself.

408
01:17:47.834 --> 01:17:51.834
A lot has to happen in our earthly life and that is not always fun.

409
01:17:51.834 --> 01:17:54.834
That is why there are sometimes problems in our lives.

410
01:17:54.834 --> 01:17:58.834
And that is why God doesn't always just solve it for you right away.

411
01:17:59.834 --> 01:18:03.834
Because God is busy preparing you for His return.

412
01:18:03.834 --> 01:18:08.834
So sometimes those problems and struggles are just necessary.

413
01:18:08.834 --> 01:18:15.834
By the way, no wait, we will first read about that.

414
01:18:16.834 --> 01:18:22.834
By the way, if you look at a few men of God throughout history.

415
01:18:22.834 --> 01:18:26.834
They also had to go through quite a bit.

416
01:18:26.834 --> 01:18:30.834
And they sometimes had to wait a long time before an answer came.

417
01:18:30.834 --> 01:18:33.834
Just think of Job.

418
01:18:33.834 --> 01:18:35.834
Job did not feel well.

419
01:18:35.834 --> 01:18:37.834
He did not feel well.

420
01:18:37.834 --> 01:18:40.834
He did not feel well.

421
01:18:41.834 --> 01:18:44.834
Just think of Job.

422
01:18:44.834 --> 01:18:46.834
Job loses everything.

423
01:18:46.834 --> 01:18:47.834
How come?

424
01:18:47.834 --> 01:18:48.834
What is God up to?

425
01:18:48.834 --> 01:18:50.834
Is God not a good Father to Job?

426
01:18:50.834 --> 01:18:51.834
Or Joseph.

427
01:18:51.834 --> 01:18:54.834
He had a dream that he would become king.

428
01:18:54.834 --> 01:18:55.834
What happens?

429
01:18:55.834 --> 01:19:01.834
He is sold by his own brother and ends up spending thirteen years in prison.

430
01:19:01.834 --> 01:19:03.834
Thirteen years in prison.

431
01:19:03.834 --> 01:19:06.834
He had a dream from God.

432
01:19:06.834 --> 01:19:08.834
He would become king.

433
01:19:08.834 --> 01:19:10.834
What is happening here?

434
01:19:10.834 --> 01:19:15.834
David was anointed by Samuel as a young man.

435
01:19:15.834 --> 01:19:18.834
You are going to be king, because he has made a mess of it.

436
01:19:18.834 --> 01:19:19.834
Oh, thinks David.

437
01:19:19.834 --> 01:19:22.834
Yes, off to Jerusalem, to the throne.

438
01:19:22.834 --> 01:19:26.834
No, for years there is a huge struggle here.

439
01:19:26.834 --> 01:19:28.834
We have talked a lot about that this year.

440
01:19:28.834 --> 01:19:31.834
Is he being pursued and hunted by Saul?

441
01:19:31.834 --> 01:19:32.834
How come?

442
01:19:32.834 --> 01:19:34.834
Why?

443
01:19:34.834 --> 01:19:41.834
Moses, called to finally free the people after 400 years from Egypt.

444
01:19:41.834 --> 01:19:51.834
He must flee for forty years before God calls him at the burning bush and he may go to the Father to set the people free.

445
01:19:51.834 --> 01:19:58.834
And then he has to wander in the desert for another forty years without them getting out.

446
01:19:59.834 --> 01:20:05.834
Even Jesus, after he was baptized, was led into the desert by the Holy Spirit.

447
01:20:05.834 --> 01:20:09.834
For forty days to be tempted by the devil.

448
01:20:09.834 --> 01:20:13.834
So God allows many things in our lives, simply.

449
01:20:13.834 --> 01:20:16.834
I don't care what you call it.

450
01:20:16.834 --> 01:20:21.834
He gives it, or the devil gives it, or you're messing things up yourself, whatever.

451
01:20:21.834 --> 01:20:26.834
But God allows many things because we simply need it.

452
01:20:26.834 --> 01:20:29.834
To grow into that perfect bride.

453
01:20:31.834 --> 01:20:34.834
And we will read in Hebrews 12.

454
01:20:36.834 --> 01:20:38.834
The purpose of this suffering.

455
01:20:38.834 --> 01:20:43.834
For our earthly fathers have raised us as well as they could for a number of years.

456
01:20:43.834 --> 01:20:47.834
But our heavenly Father knows what is truly good for us.

457
01:20:47.834 --> 01:20:52.834
He raises us with the intention that we will be just as delighted as He is.

458
01:20:52.834 --> 01:20:54.834
That's this, right?

459
01:20:54.834 --> 01:20:56.834
If He disciplines us...

460
01:20:56.834 --> 01:20:59.834
How come God disciplines us?

461
01:20:59.834 --> 01:21:04.834
When he punishes us, it is not pleasant at the moment, but painful.

462
01:21:04.834 --> 01:21:08.834
But in the end, it produces something good.

463
01:21:08.834 --> 01:21:13.834
For if we are obedient to the upbringing of our Father...

464
01:21:14.834 --> 01:21:18.834
Ruben just mentioned that for us as well.

465
01:21:18.834 --> 01:21:23.834
Be obedient, do not run away when God leads you into temptations.

466
01:21:23.834 --> 01:21:26.834
But be obedient and walk in His way.

467
01:21:26.834 --> 01:21:28.834
Then He will be pleased with us.

468
01:21:28.834 --> 01:21:31.834
So be brave and take charge of yourself.

469
01:21:31.834 --> 01:21:33.834
Live as God wants.

470
01:21:33.834 --> 01:21:37.834
Then your faith will not become weaker, but rather stronger.

471
01:21:37.834 --> 01:21:40.834
That is of course very important.

472
01:21:40.834 --> 01:21:43.834
Through those struggles, we will become stronger.

473
01:21:43.834 --> 01:21:49.834
Just like weak legs that are used well, become stronger.

474
01:21:51.834 --> 01:21:53.834
And then Romans 5.

475
01:21:55.834 --> 01:21:57.834
But that is not the only thing.

476
01:21:57.834 --> 01:22:00.834
We are also happy when we are having a hard time.

477
01:22:00.834 --> 01:22:03.834
Okay, who is happy when they are having a hard time?

478
01:22:04.834 --> 01:22:07.834
A few dare to raise their hand.

479
01:22:08.834 --> 01:22:10.834
That is a struggle.

480
01:22:10.834 --> 01:22:13.834
It is not fun when you are in difficulties.

481
01:22:13.834 --> 01:22:16.834
When it doesn't all go so easily.

482
01:22:18.834 --> 01:22:20.834
Let's see, Romans then.

483
01:22:20.834 --> 01:22:24.834
Paul dares to say here that we should be glad.

484
01:22:25.834 --> 01:22:27.834
How can we be glad when things are difficult?

485
01:22:27.834 --> 01:22:29.834
Well, because...

486
01:22:29.834 --> 01:22:31.834
Let's read on.

487
01:22:32.834 --> 01:22:35.834
For through difficulties we learn to persevere.

488
01:22:35.834 --> 01:22:39.834
And as we learn to persevere, our spirit becomes strong.

489
01:22:39.834 --> 01:22:44.834
And as our spirit becomes strong, we learn to trust more and more in God.

490
01:22:44.834 --> 01:22:50.834
So you see that difficulties lead us to come closer to God.

491
01:22:50.834 --> 01:22:53.834
That we become more and more that beautiful bride form.

492
01:22:53.834 --> 01:22:58.834
You see that we shouldn't just avoid troubles when they arise.

493
01:22:58.834 --> 01:23:02.834
You see that it makes sense and is necessary.

494
01:23:02.834 --> 01:23:05.834
And that you can even be glad and thankful for it.

495
01:23:05.834 --> 01:23:07.834
And this is a mystery.

496
01:23:07.834 --> 01:23:11.834
You don't learn this just on the first day after you come to know Jesus.

497
01:23:11.834 --> 01:23:13.834
But as you walk with him...

498
01:23:13.834 --> 01:23:19.834
you will find out that God hasn't just flipped a switch after your repentance.

499
01:23:19.834 --> 01:23:23.834
And that your little life doesn't just become one big kingdom of peace.

500
01:23:23.834 --> 01:23:27.834
But then you realize that you are still just like all other people in the world...

501
01:23:27.834 --> 01:23:29.834
you have to go through a lot of things.

502
01:23:29.834 --> 01:23:35.834
Only when your perspective becomes that you see what it is for.

503
01:23:35.834 --> 01:23:38.834
Where that leads to, where you are headed.

504
01:23:38.834 --> 01:23:40.834
Then you can even be happy about it.

505
01:23:40.834 --> 01:23:42.834
And God says, Erik doesn't like it.

506
01:23:42.834 --> 01:23:44.834
Then you can just talk to God.

507
01:23:44.834 --> 01:23:46.834
You can even be angry with God.

508
01:23:46.834 --> 01:23:47.834
That's all fine.

509
01:23:47.834 --> 01:23:49.834
But as long as you talk to Him about it.

510
01:23:49.834 --> 01:23:55.834
As long as you are engaged with Him and make sure that your problems...

511
01:23:56.834 --> 01:24:03.834
bring you closer to God and train you in the bridal relationship.

512
01:24:06.834 --> 01:24:10.834
He is preparing us as His bride.

513
01:24:10.834 --> 01:24:12.834
We are His fiancées.

514
01:24:14.834 --> 01:24:17.834
God is not indifferent at all.

515
01:24:17.834 --> 01:24:21.834
You cannot say that God is not interested.

516
01:24:21.834 --> 01:24:24.834
You certainly cannot say that God does nothing about it.

517
01:24:25.834 --> 01:24:28.834
God knows you inside and out.

518
01:24:28.834 --> 01:24:31.834
You are extremely precious to Him.

519
01:24:31.834 --> 01:24:33.834
He is a good Father.

520
01:24:33.834 --> 01:24:35.834
He has the very best in store for you.

521
01:24:35.834 --> 01:24:40.834
He does not let you stay in problems a second longer than necessary.

522
01:24:40.834 --> 01:24:45.834
He is busy purifying you, refining you, pruning you, sanctifying you.

523
01:24:45.834 --> 01:24:48.834
To ensure that you become perfect for him.

524
01:24:48.834 --> 01:24:50.834
That is what he is working on.

525
01:24:50.834 --> 01:24:52.834
That is his perspective.

526
01:24:52.834 --> 01:24:55.834
So if we focus too much on our earthly problems...

527
01:24:55.834 --> 01:24:58.834
we are looking in completely the wrong direction.

528
01:24:58.834 --> 01:25:02.834
We need to see what Jesus is doing in us and with us.

529
01:25:02.834 --> 01:25:06.834
So never say, why is God not doing anything about it?

530
01:25:06.834 --> 01:25:08.834
He is doing everything about it.

531
01:25:08.834 --> 01:25:10.834
He died on a cross for you.

532
01:25:10.834 --> 01:25:12.834
You are so precious to him.

533
01:25:12.834 --> 01:25:15.834
He would rather be tortured to death himself...

534
01:25:15.834 --> 01:25:18.834
than for you to be lost forever.

535
01:25:18.834 --> 01:25:22.834
So his eye is completely on your redemption, on your salvation...

536
01:25:22.834 --> 01:25:25.834
on your being with him forever and ever.

537
01:25:25.834 --> 01:25:30.834
We just read, all pain, all tears, death, all misery...

538
01:25:30.834 --> 01:25:33.834
he will take away when we marry him.

539
01:25:33.834 --> 01:25:37.834
But until that time we still have to go through things.

540
01:25:38.834 --> 01:25:44.834
I want to make an important nuance.

541
01:25:44.834 --> 01:25:51.834
Not all problems are from God, for God, or to God.

542
01:25:51.834 --> 01:25:54.834
You can also be in a problem...

543
01:25:54.834 --> 01:25:58.834
because you are just making a mess of things.

544
01:25:58.834 --> 01:26:01.834
Through your sins, by being disobedient...

545
01:26:01.834 --> 01:26:04.834
by your responsibility.

546
01:26:04.834 --> 01:26:08.834
Through your sins, by being disobedient to God.

547
01:26:10.834 --> 01:26:13.834
By being involved in wrong things.

548
01:26:13.834 --> 01:26:15.834
By not listening to God.

549
01:26:15.834 --> 01:26:19.834
By not going to Him with your problems.

550
01:26:21.834 --> 01:26:24.834
And not listening to His voice.

551
01:26:24.834 --> 01:26:29.834
For often when you are in trouble, God also gives you a task.

552
01:26:29.834 --> 01:26:32.834
He does not just flip a switch.

553
01:26:32.834 --> 01:26:35.834
He is on a journey with you somewhere.

554
01:26:35.834 --> 01:26:38.834
And so He will show you the way.

555
01:26:38.834 --> 01:26:41.834
For this, the Holy Spirit had to come.

556
01:26:41.834 --> 01:26:44.834
The Holy Spirit in us shows us the way.

557
01:26:44.834 --> 01:26:47.834
So when we are in trouble and cry out to Him...

558
01:26:47.834 --> 01:26:51.834
why this misery, why this struggle...

559
01:26:51.834 --> 01:26:54.834
then He often gives an answer.

560
01:26:54.834 --> 01:26:58.834
And it may just be that you have gotten yourself into a mess...

561
01:26:58.834 --> 01:27:02.834
or that he has put you in a bind for his purpose.

562
01:27:02.834 --> 01:27:06.834
It may simply be that you, through your sins or stubbornness or disobedience...

563
01:27:06.834 --> 01:27:09.834
just remain stuck in the struggle.

564
01:27:09.834 --> 01:27:12.834
And that he has long been trying to make it clear to you...

565
01:27:12.834 --> 01:27:16.834
what you need to change so that you can get out of it.

566
01:27:17.834 --> 01:27:19.834
So that is a bit of nuance.

567
01:27:19.834 --> 01:27:23.834
Not all misery and difficulties and troubles are just from God.

568
01:27:23.834 --> 01:27:28.834
But he always uses it to bring us closer to him.

569
01:27:35.834 --> 01:27:37.834
Hosanna is not wrong.

570
01:27:40.834 --> 01:27:44.834
I also did not name the sermon Maranatha instead of Hosanna...

571
01:27:44.834 --> 01:27:48.834
but I named it from Hosanna to Maranatha.

572
01:27:48.834 --> 01:27:52.834
It is okay to cry out to God when you are in difficulties.

573
01:27:53.834 --> 01:27:56.834
When you are in the struggle. God likes that.

574
01:27:56.834 --> 01:28:00.834
If you are his bride, he wants nothing more...

575
01:28:00.834 --> 01:28:03.834
than to hear from you when you are having a hard time.

576
01:28:03.834 --> 01:28:08.834
So Hosanna, save me, help me, is completely okay.

577
01:28:09.834 --> 01:28:11.834
But not without Maranatha.

578
01:28:12.834 --> 01:28:14.834
We see a lot of this in David.

579
01:28:14.834 --> 01:28:17.834
David is the writer of many psalms.

580
01:28:17.834 --> 01:28:19.834
And in many psalms...

581
01:28:19.834 --> 01:28:21.834
David had a tremendously difficult time.

582
01:28:21.834 --> 01:28:27.834
He was pursued so relentlessly by Saul that he was constantly in danger of his life.

583
01:28:27.834 --> 01:28:29.834
And he cried out to God.

584
01:28:29.834 --> 01:28:31.834
You see that in many psalms.

585
01:28:31.834 --> 01:28:34.834
That he cries out to God in his misery.

586
01:28:34.834 --> 01:28:36.834
Why, how much longer?

587
01:28:36.834 --> 01:28:38.834
Why are you doing nothing about it?

588
01:28:38.834 --> 01:28:41.834
Let's take psalm 13, for example.

589
01:28:48.834 --> 01:28:51.834
How long will I still be in trouble...

590
01:28:51.834 --> 01:28:54.834
and will I worry every day?

591
01:28:54.834 --> 01:28:57.834
How much longer will my enemy be stronger than I?

592
01:28:57.834 --> 01:29:00.834
Lord my God, see what is happening.

593
01:29:00.834 --> 01:29:04.834
Answer me. Please give me new hope again.

594
01:29:04.834 --> 01:29:06.834
Do not let me die yet.

595
01:29:07.834 --> 01:29:12.834
That is his Hosanna cry to God, help me.

596
01:29:12.834 --> 01:29:14.834
But then he continues.

597
01:29:14.834 --> 01:29:16.834
For he does not stop there.

598
01:29:16.834 --> 01:29:20.834
He continues. He says, I trust in your goodness and your love.

599
01:29:20.834 --> 01:29:24.834
My heart rejoices, because I am certain that you will save me.

600
01:29:24.834 --> 01:29:29.834
I sing for my Lord, because he has been good to me.

601
01:29:31.834 --> 01:29:34.834
You see this repeatedly in the psalms of David.

602
01:29:34.834 --> 01:29:36.834
He cries out in distress to God.

603
01:29:36.834 --> 01:29:39.834
In his Hosanna, help me Lord.

604
01:29:39.834 --> 01:29:42.834
But he always ends it with Maranatha.

605
01:29:42.834 --> 01:29:44.834
Come Lord Jesus.

606
01:29:44.834 --> 01:29:46.834
A longing love for him.

607
01:29:46.834 --> 01:29:48.834
A knowing that God is good.

608
01:29:48.834 --> 01:29:51.834
And that God will not forsake him.

609
01:29:51.834 --> 01:29:53.834
And that is so important.

610
01:29:53.834 --> 01:29:56.834
We must learn that.

611
01:29:56.834 --> 01:29:59.834
That we do not only see God as our helper.

612
01:29:59.834 --> 01:30:03.834
Our vending machine, just put in a quarter.

613
01:30:03.834 --> 01:30:05.834
And God will solve everything.

614
01:30:05.834 --> 01:30:09.834
But God who is our bridegroom.

615
01:30:09.834 --> 01:30:11.834
And we are his bride, his betrothed.

616
01:30:12.834 --> 01:30:16.834
And we who are focused on him and long for him.

617
01:30:18.834 --> 01:30:24.834
Our focus must be on that wedding that is to come.

618
01:30:26.834 --> 01:30:31.834
The band may come on stage.

619
01:30:32.834 --> 01:30:34.834
Hallelujah.

620
01:30:35.834 --> 01:30:40.834
Imagine an earthly betrothed.

621
01:30:40.834 --> 01:30:43.834
Are there any engaged people here?

622
01:30:43.834 --> 01:30:45.834
No one? Yes.

623
01:30:47.834 --> 01:30:49.834
Congratulations.

624
01:30:49.834 --> 01:30:52.834
Because marriage is so precious.

625
01:30:52.834 --> 01:30:55.834
But imagine, you have a fiancée.

626
01:30:55.834 --> 01:30:57.834
And she doesn't take it all that seriously.

627
01:30:57.834 --> 01:31:00.834
She does want to marry you.

628
01:31:00.834 --> 01:31:05.834
But well, you're not that interesting otherwise.

629
01:31:05.834 --> 01:31:09.834
And there are so many other fun interesting things in the world.

630
01:31:09.834 --> 01:31:12.834
She commits adultery and then comes back.

631
01:31:12.834 --> 01:31:14.834
And sorry.

632
01:31:14.834 --> 01:31:17.834
Imagine such a fiancée.

633
01:31:18.834 --> 01:31:21.834
Now imagine the congregation.

634
01:31:21.834 --> 01:31:23.834
As his fiancée.

635
01:31:23.834 --> 01:31:28.834
Now imagine your sin and your disobedience and your struggles.

636
01:31:30.834 --> 01:31:34.834
Jesus would have every right to say, figure it all out yourself.

637
01:31:34.834 --> 01:31:37.834
I will marry someone else.

638
01:31:37.834 --> 01:31:39.834
But he doesn't do that.

639
01:31:39.834 --> 01:31:41.834
Because he loves you so much.

640
01:31:41.834 --> 01:31:43.834
He is so longing for you.

641
01:31:43.834 --> 01:31:47.834
So he seeks you, he forgives you time and again.

642
01:31:47.834 --> 01:31:50.834
But you don't automatically end up with him.

643
01:31:50.834 --> 01:31:53.834
If you remain stuck in your earthly focus.

644
01:31:53.834 --> 01:31:56.834
If you remain stuck in your sin.

645
01:31:56.834 --> 01:32:00.834
If you remain stuck in avoiding problems.

646
01:32:00.834 --> 01:32:05.834
If you remain stuck wanting to lead a nice, pleasant, comfortable earthly life.

647
01:32:05.834 --> 01:32:09.834
And do not pay the price to move towards Jesus.

648
01:32:09.834 --> 01:32:11.834
Then you will not end up with him.

649
01:32:11.834 --> 01:32:14.834
Then you will not be part of the bride.

650
01:32:14.834 --> 01:32:17.834
Of the bride who will marry Jesus.

651
01:32:17.834 --> 01:32:19.834
So take it seriously.

652
01:32:21.834 --> 01:32:24.834
Do not be such an unfaithful fiancée.

653
01:32:24.834 --> 01:32:28.834
But be a loving fiancée for Jesus.

654
01:32:28.834 --> 01:32:30.834
Seek his heart.

655
01:32:30.834 --> 01:32:32.834
Do not seek his hand.

656
01:32:32.834 --> 01:32:34.834
Do not seek what he can do for you.

657
01:32:34.834 --> 01:32:36.834
But seek his heart.

658
01:32:36.834 --> 01:32:37.834
Seek his love.

659
01:32:37.834 --> 01:32:39.834
Interact with his love.

660
01:32:39.834 --> 01:32:44.834
We will conclude with the very last verse of the Bible.

661
01:32:46.834 --> 01:32:50.834
I find it so incredibly amazing that the Bible ends like this.

662
01:32:50.834 --> 01:32:54.834
These are literally the last verses of the Bible.

663
01:32:54.834 --> 01:32:56.834
This is the final destination.

664
01:32:56.834 --> 01:32:59.834
This is why we are here on earth.

665
01:32:59.834 --> 01:33:02.834
This is where we are all heading.

666
01:33:02.834 --> 01:33:05.834
This is the great climax.

667
01:33:05.834 --> 01:33:07.834
This is our eternal life.

668
01:33:07.834 --> 01:33:09.834
The Spirit and the bride.

669
01:33:09.834 --> 01:33:11.834
The Spirit is the Holy Spirit.

670
01:33:11.834 --> 01:33:15.834
So beautiful that He is fully involved here as well.

671
01:33:15.834 --> 01:33:16.834
The Spirit and the bride.

672
01:33:16.834 --> 01:33:17.834
We are the bride.

673
01:33:17.834 --> 01:33:19.834
The congregation of Jesus.

674
01:33:19.834 --> 01:33:22.834
The Spirit and the bride say come.

675
01:33:22.834 --> 01:33:24.834
Maranatha.

676
01:33:24.834 --> 01:33:27.834
And let everyone who hears say come.

677
01:33:27.834 --> 01:33:29.834
Anyone who thirsts may come.

678
01:33:29.834 --> 01:33:33.834
Anyone who wishes may come and drink of the water that gives life.

679
01:33:33.834 --> 01:33:36.834
You don't have to pay anything for it.

680
01:33:36.834 --> 01:33:40.834
He who has spoken these things says.

681
01:33:40.834 --> 01:33:42.834
Jesus says yes.

682
01:33:42.834 --> 01:33:44.834
I will come soon.

683
01:33:44.834 --> 01:33:45.834
Amen.

684
01:33:45.834 --> 01:33:47.834
So it is.

685
01:33:47.834 --> 01:33:48.834
Yes.

686
01:33:48.834 --> 01:33:50.834
Come here Jesus.

687
01:33:50.834 --> 01:33:51.834
Yes.

688
01:33:51.834 --> 01:33:53.834
Maranatha.

689
01:33:53.834 --> 01:33:54.834
Come here Jesus.

690
01:33:54.834 --> 01:33:57.834
Shall we stand up?

691
01:33:57.834 --> 01:33:59.834
Come here Jesus.

692
01:33:59.834 --> 01:34:01.834
We long for you Lord.

693
01:34:01.834 --> 01:34:03.834
We want to be your bride.

694
01:34:03.834 --> 01:34:05.834
We want to be your fiancée.

695
01:34:05.834 --> 01:34:08.834
We want to take it very seriously.

696
01:34:08.834 --> 01:34:14.834
To be the best fiancée for you that can possibly exist.

697
01:34:14.834 --> 01:34:16.834
You are so worth it Jesus.

698
01:34:16.834 --> 01:34:21.834
The perfect, the holy, pure love.

699
01:34:21.834 --> 01:34:23.834
You are so worth it Jesus.

700
01:34:23.834 --> 01:34:27.834
That you receive a perfect bride without spot or wrinkle.

701
01:34:27.834 --> 01:34:32.834
Here we are, Lord.

702
01:34:32.834 --> 01:34:33.834
As your fiancée.

703
01:34:33.834 --> 01:34:35.834
Sorry, Lord.

704
01:34:35.834 --> 01:34:41.834
That we are not yet that beautiful bride that you are so worthy of.

705
01:34:41.834 --> 01:34:43.834
But we do want to, Lord.

706
01:34:43.834 --> 01:34:46.834
Our heart's desire goes out to you, Lord.

707
01:34:46.834 --> 01:34:47.834
Help us, Lord.

708
01:34:47.834 --> 01:34:53.834
To go through this earthly life in all our struggles and everything we go through.

709
01:34:53.834 --> 01:34:56.834
Help us not to be focused on the earth.

710
01:34:56.834 --> 01:34:58.834
But to be focused on heaven.

711
01:34:58.834 --> 01:35:03.834
Help us to be focused on the wedding that is to come.

712
01:35:03.834 --> 01:35:09.834
Help us above all to be focused on you, dear Jesus.

713
01:35:09.834 --> 01:35:11.834
We love you, Lord.

714
01:35:11.834 --> 01:35:13.834
We long for you, Lord.

715
01:35:13.834 --> 01:35:16.834
We want to be with you forever, Lord.

716
01:35:16.834 --> 01:35:19.834
We long for the misery to be over.

717
01:35:19.834 --> 01:35:23.834
But above all, we long for you yourself.

718
01:35:23.834 --> 01:35:27.834
Dear Jesus, come soon.

719
01:35:42.834 --> 01:35:45.834
You can do it.

720
01:35:45.834 --> 01:35:49.834
The whole world.

721
01:35:49.834 --> 01:35:52.834
You can do it.

722
01:35:52.834 --> 01:35:56.834
The whole world.

723
01:35:56.834 --> 01:36:03.834
Give me Jesus.

724
